& [BoundaryFormation] separates supplied-byte derivation from physical acquisition
  + [inside] strict plan decoding, private streaming SHA-256 state, checked chunk and byte accounting, consuming finalization, output-only content observation, and revalidated stability binding
  + [outside] file opening, handle ownership, physical read order, paths, clocks, platform calls, filesystem facts, traversal, Git projection, receipts, admission, mutation, sealing, cleanup, and promotion
  + [supplied_chunk] means only one byte slice passed by the caller to one transition
  + [derived_digest] means SHA-256 of the exact ordered concatenation accepted by that accumulator
  + [stable_binding] means value agreement with one newly reconciled supplied stable pair, not physical byte provenance

& [AtomicRequirementSet] is complete
  + [M2B-SCD-001] require exact profile, nonzero local identities, bounded scalar values, strict JSON, and a 4096-byte encoded-plan cap
  + [M2B-SCD-002] create private accumulator state only after complete plan validation and expose no successful-observation constructor
  + [M2B-SCD-003] make each chunk transition consuming, reject empty chunks, and return no resumable state on failure
  + [M2B-SCD-004] use checked chunk and byte arithmetic before mutating SHA-256 state and enforce exact plan budgets
  + [M2B-SCD-005] hash only accepted bytes in supplied order without framing, normalization, decoding, retention, or delimiter insertion
  + [M2B-SCD-006] represent empty content as zero chunks and derive the standard SHA-256 digest of the empty byte string
  + [M2B-SCD-007] consume the accumulator at finalization and require exact observed-to-expected length equality
  + [M2B-SCD-008] release one serializable, inspectable, externally nonconstructible and nondeserializable supplied-content observation
  + [M2B-SCD-009] bind only by invoking the current supplied-entry stability reconciler over its input
  + [M2B-SCD-010] require regular_file, exact entry-reference equality, and exact pre/post EOF equality to both expected and observed lengths
  + [M2B-SCD-011] preserve the complete content observation and complete stable pair in one output-only binding
  + [M2B-SCD-012] return one closed bounded atomic fault with exact nested stability fault only for the stability class
  + [M2B-SCD-013] deny physical, temporal, platform, origin, completeness, freshness, immutability, content-stability, and downstream claims
  + [M2B-SCD-014] preserve zero effect, zero unsafe, zero Cargo delta, and complete focused, static, evidence, global, and quality proof

& [PlanModel] is strict source data
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-content-digest/0.1
  + [content_read_identity] is caller-owned nonzero u64 local syntax
  + [entry_reference_identity] is caller-owned nonzero u64 expected at later binding
  + [expected_content_length] is u64 and may be zero
  + [maximum_content_bytes] is positive u64 at most 1099511627776
  + [maximum_chunks] is positive u32 at most 1048576
  + [relation] expected_content_length is not greater than maximum_content_bytes
  + [encoded_plan_cap] is exactly 4096 bytes before serde decoding
  - never: accept chunks, paths, handles, digest text, clocks, or unknown fields in the plan

& [AccumulatorModel] is private constant-size derived state
  + [state] is validated plan, Sha256 state, observed_length u64, and observed_chunks u32
  + [construction] is available only through validated begin or decode-and-begin entry points
  + [inspection] may expose immutable plan and counter getters
  + [transition] consumes self and returns Result of next self or fault
  + [mutation_order] calculates and validates next counters before updating the hasher
  + [storage] retains no supplied content chunks
  - never: implement Clone, Serialize, or Deserialize for accumulator state

& [ChunkTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [nonempty_within_all_limits] increments checked counters, hashes exact bytes, and returns next accumulator
  + [empty] returns chunk fault and consumes prior accumulator
  + [chunk_count_overflow_or_limit] returns limit or resource fault before hash update
  + [byte_count_overflow] returns resource fault before hash update
  + [expected_length_excess] returns length fault before hash update
  + [maximum_content_excess] returns limit fault before hash update
  + [usize_to_u64_failure] returns resource fault before hash update

& [FinalizationTruthTable] is exhaustive
  + [observed_equals_expected] finalizes once and returns exact lowercase 64-character SHA-256 observation
  + [zero_expected_zero_chunks] returns SHA-256 e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855
  + [observed_below_expected] returns length fault and no observation
  + [observed_above_expected] cannot arise from an admitted transition
  + [repeatability] equal concatenated bytes produce equal digest regardless of valid chunk partition while accounting for actual chunk count

& [ObservationModel] is derived output only
  + [fields] are profile, content-read identity, entry-reference identity, expected length, observed length, maximum-content budget, maximum-chunk budget, observed chunk count, and derived digest
  + [construction] is private to successful consuming finalization
  + [public_surface] is Serialize plus immutable getters
  - never: derive Deserialize, expose public fields, provide Default, or provide a public constructor

& [BindingTruthTable] is exact
  + [stability_rejects] returns stability fault preserving the exact nested fault
  + [stable_kind_directory] returns kind fault
  + [entry_reference_differs] returns entry_reference fault
  + [pre_EOF_differs_from_content_length] returns metadata_length fault
  + [post_EOF_differs_from_content_length] returns metadata_length fault
  + [all_gates_pass] returns complete observation plus complete stable pair
  - never: accept WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair directly or reconstruct only part of it

& [FaultModel] is closed and bounded
  + [codes] are json, profile, content_read_identity, entry_reference_identity, limit, chunk, length, stability, kind, entry_reference, metadata_length, and resource
  + [nested_stability_fault] is present exactly for stability and absent otherwise
  + [field] is a closed implementation-selected string no longer than 64 Unicode scalar values
  + [message] is no longer than 256 Unicode scalar values
  + [atomicity] every failure returns no content observation, binding, or resumable failed accumulator
  - never: disclose supplied bytes, hash state, or encoded unbounded nested input

& [DataDesignModel] separates authority layers
  + [source_data] is validated plan plus borrowed supplied chunks plus later stability input
  + [derived_state] is private hasher and checked counters
  + [derived_observation] is output-only evidence about supplied bytes
  + [prerequisite_derived_input] is a stable pair recreated through the existing reconciler
  + [derived_binding] is structural agreement between the two derived records
  + [physical_data] is absent
  + [persistence] is absent
  + [global_identity] is absent

& [IdentityDiscipline] keeps namespaces local
  + [content_read_identity] is unique only as far as the caller guarantees within unstated caller scope
  + [entry_reference_identity] is syntax joined to the existing local reconciliation namespace
  + [stability_reconciliation_identity] and batch identities are preserved from the stable pair
  + [identity_stability_window] is the immediate values supplied to the pure functions
  - never: infer authenticated, global, durable, physical, process, handle, or filesystem identity

& [ConceptualLogicalPhysicalSeparation] is explicit
  + [conceptual] account for exact caller-supplied bytes and compare their declared length/reference against stable supplied metadata
  + [logical] plan to accumulator transitions to observation, then stability input to stable pair to binding
  + [physical] safe in-memory Rust using sha2 and serde only
  + [future_physical] a separately authorized producer may later supply bytes and stability inputs

